    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d72">

                <pb facs="0231" n="203" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v11/pg203"/>

                <head>72. Telegram From the Mission to the United Nations to the Department of
                        State<anchor n="0" xml:id="d72-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>New York</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1962-10-25T14:30:00-04:00">October 25, 1962,
                            2:30 p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1459. Subject:SC on Cuba.</p>
                <p>I saw U Thant this morning and conveyed to him suggestions contained in Deptel
                    1084 (USUN 4963).<anchor n="1" xml:id="d72-f2"/> He said he would transmit
                    suggestions to Khrushchev in form of confidential message.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d72-f3"/> He would also send President Kennedy note reporting his
                    message to Khrushchev and asking that US exercise restraint in
                    circumstances.</p>
                <p>Thant told me Zorin asked him at 7:30 last night what Thant appeal in Council was
                    going to say. Thant replied that it was based on his appeal to Khrushchev and
                    Kennedy. Zorin said he had not received it. After Thant explained to Zorin
                    nature of his appeal, Zorin replied that it was very bad proposal, since
                    blockade was wholly illegal and that Thant should be concerned with legality and
                    should not equate lifting quarantine with stopping ships going to Cuba. Thant
                    replied he was not concerned with legality, but with averting a crisis.</p>
                <p>Thant told me that Afro-Asians were putting great pressure on Zorin to accept,
                    but that on basis of Zorin’s preliminary reaction Thant <pb facs="0232" n="204"
                        xml:id="pg204"/> expects negative reply. Thant anticipates long legal attack
                    on the quarantine.</p>
                <p>If both sides accept his suspension proposal this afternoon, he thinks SC should
                    recess pending discussion on modalities. Parties should then report what
                    agreement they have reached on modalities and thereafter substantive
                    negotiations could take place without another Council meeting.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Stevenson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
